{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me verify with the public test plus my own comprehensive checks. I'll run the public test and a heredoc inline test.\n\nTest cases:\n1. Public: feed(b'{\"a\":1}\\n') == [{\"a\":1}]\n2. Record split: feed(b'{\"a\":') == [] ; feed(b'1}\\n') == [{\"a\":1}]\n3. UTF-8 codepoint split: b'{\"k\":\"\\xc3' then b'\\xa9\"}\\n' → [{\"k\":\"é\"}]\n4. Emoji split at every byte boundary.\n5. Blank lines ignored: b'\\n\\n \\t \\n'.\n6. Multiple records per chunk, records split across many chunks (byte-by-byte).\n7. CRLF.\n8. No premature emission of number prefix: b'12' then b'3\\n' → [123] not [12, 3].\n9. Fuzz: random JSON objects, serialize to lines, feed chunked at random boundaries; compare to reference list.\n10. Byte-by-byte feeding of a fuzz corpus compared to whole-feed result.\n11. Performance: 2MB record fed in 4KB chunks, time it (ensure not quadratic - could compare with timing rough).\n12. Invalid JSON raises JSONDecodeError? Let's check it raises.\n13. Empty chunk returns [].\n\nLet me build a test script inline. Use python3 - <<'EOF'.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll verify against the public test and a comprehensive set of boundary cases, including byte-by-byte UTF-8 splits, fuzzing against a reference parser, and a performance check."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00082]","name":"shell_command","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/flashbench_deepseek_v41/t02 && python3 test_public.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, random, time\nfrom stream import JsonlStream\n\ndef collect(chunks):\n    s = JsonlStream(); out = []\n    for c in chunks:\n        out.extend(s.feed(c))\n    return out\n\n# 1. record split across chunks, nothing emitted prematurely\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'{\"a\":') == []\nassert s.feed(b'1}\\n') == [{\"a\": 1}]\n\n# 2. numeric prefix must not be emitted early (12 vs 123)\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'12') == []\nassert s.feed(b'3\\n') == [123]\n\n# 3. UTF-8 codepoint split\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'{\"k\":\"\\xc3') == []\nassert s.feed(b'\\xa9\"}\\n') == [{\"k\": \"\\u00e9\"}]\n\n# 4. emoji split at EVERY byte boundary\nrec = json.dumps({\"e\": \"\\U0001F600\"}, ensure_ascii=False).encode() + b\"\\n\"\nfor i in range(len(rec) + 1):\n    assert collect([rec[:i], rec[i:]]) == [{\"e\": \"\\U0001F600\"}], (i, rec[:i], rec[i:])\n\n# 5. blank lines ignored (empty, spaces, tabs, CR)\nassert collect([b'\\n\\n \\t \\n', b'{\"a\":1}\\n', b'\\r\\n']) == [{\"a\": 1}]\n\n# 6. CRLF records\nassert collect([b'{\"a\":1}\\r\\n', b'{\"b\":2}\\r\\n']) == [{\"a\": 1}, {\"b\": 2}]\n\n# 7. multiple records in one chunk + trailing partial retained\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n{\"c\"') == [{\"a\": 1}, {\"b\": 2}]\nassert s.feed(b':3}\\n') == [{\"c\": 3}]\n\n# 8. byte-by-byte feed\nrecs = [{\"i\": i, \"s\": \"héllo\\U0001F600\"} for i in range(50)]\nblob = b\"\".join(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False).encode() + b\"\\n\" for r in recs)\nassert collect([blob[i:i+1] for i in range(len(blob))]) == recs\nassert collect([bytes([b]) for b in blob]) == recs\n\n# 9. random fuzz vs reference\nrng = random.Random(1234)\nfor trial in range(200):\n    n = rng.randint(0, 12)\n    vals = [{\"k\": rng.randint(-10**6, 10**6), \"s\": \"\".join(rng.choice(\"aé\\u00e9\\U0001F600\\\"\") for _ in range(rng.randint(0, 8)))} for _ in range(n)]\n    blob = b\"\".join(json.dumps(v, ensure_ascii=False).encode() + rng.choice([b\"\\n\", b\"\\r\\n\", b\"\\n\\n\"]) for v in vals)\n    bounds = sorted(rng.randrange(len(blob) + 1) for _ in range(rng.randint(0, 10))) if blob else [0]\n    chunks, prev = [], 0\n    for b in bounds + [len(blob)]:\n        chunks.append(blob[prev:b]); prev = b\n    assert collect(chunks) == vals, (trial, vals, chunks)\n    # full blob in one shot and one chunk per record agree\n    assert collect([blob]) == vals\n\n# 10. invalid JSON still raises\nfor bad in [b'{\"a\":}\\n', b'nope\\n']:\n    try:\n        collect([bad]); raise AssertionError(\"expected exception for %r\" % bad)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        pass\n\n# 11. empty feeds are no-ops\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'') == [] and s.feed(bytearray()) == []\nassert s.feed(bytearray(b'{\"a\":1}\\n')) == [{\"a\": 1}]\n\n# 12. large record in many medium chunks: must be linear-ish and correct\nbig = {\"data\": \"x\" * 4_000_000}\nblob = json.dumps(big).encode() + b\"\\n\"\ns = JsonlStream(); t = time.time()\nfor i in range(0, len(blob), 4096):\n    res = s.feed(blob[i:i+4096])\nassert res == [big] and s.feed(b'\\n{\"z\":0}\\n') == [{\"z\": 0}]\nprint(\"ALL_OK  big-record-seconds=%.3f\" % (time.time() - t))\nEOF","description":"Run public test and comprehensive verification suite","timeout":120000}}]}}
